N42fNmMciL7" class="rte-styled-text"><span class="font-FFFFFFFF cc-rte-styled rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-p5AdKLmcda9I">ADVERTORIAL</span></span></span></div><!-- Navigation --><nav class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100 py-6 px-6 flex justify-center sticky top-0 z-50 w-full" href="" id="cc-id-GImS4E7H2fBo" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1777371042438_1.webp"><span class="serif-font text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight" href="" id="cc-id-iN79qMjwzIhR">FINDING MY GLOW</span></nav><!-- Main Content --><main class="w-full px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-20 bg-white" href="" id="cc-id-uo8MqQteEbB6"><!-- HEADLINE SECTION --><header class="pt-12 pb-10 text-center max-w-6xl mx-auto" href="" id="cc-id-bYqyxacL30tW"><span class="bg-red-600 text-white px-6 py-2 text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded-sm mb-8 inline-block" href="" id="cc-id-j6QfzFWpBInq" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1777371042438_1.webp">Trending this week</span><h1 class="text-5xl md:text-7xl font-bold leading-tight mb-8 text-gray-900 serif-font" href="" id="cc-id-Roy80vWeJ9mb">
                                Top Dermatologist Warns: Dark Spots 2x’s Every
                                Year After Menopause - Only This
                                <span class="font-E779C7FF cc-rte-styled rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-FKRVhts4AgwT"><span class="font-B56566FF cc-rte-styled rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-fUcGKLhUYjWc">“Stanford Peptide”</span></span>
                                Finally Shuts Them Off For Good
                              </h1><p class="text-gray-500 text-xl md:text-2xl leading-relaxed mb-8 px-4 font-medium" href="" id="cc-id-6wVxqQFp5sDs">
                                100,000+ women over 40 have reversed years of
                                sun damage and age spots with this
                                dermatologist's simple daily ritual — without
                                hydroquinone, harsh chemicals, or lasers.
                              </p><div class="flex items-center justify-center space-x-6 text-lg text-gray-400 border-t border-b border-gray-100 py-5 w-full max-w-2xl mx-auto" href="" id="cc-id-BHfgUtKe6kBz"><div class="flex items-center" href="" id="cc-id-YwSz63JpKfug"><img src="{{ '1777390722143_0.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="Editor" class="rounded-full w-10 h-10 mr-4 fk-disable-lazy" href="" id="cc-id-B876ri3E5E2Y" title="" onclick="" target="_self" align="center" width="" height=""><span class="font-semibold text-gray-600" href="" id="cc-id-NUE878ATshsm">Dr. Amanda Pierce</span></div><span href="" id="cc-id-0ByUlU2ozfDg">•</span><span href="" id="cc-id-zabc7Dw9NJJL">4 Min Read</span><span href="" id="cc-id-fiogdobDcH93">•</span><span href="" id="cc-id-mUMeOKVPEBlQ">Updated Today</span></div></header><div class="relative w-full mb-12 max-w-7xl mx-auto" href="" id="cc-id-LJgRsLfhGgex"><img src="{{ '1778134027741_derm_pres_5_4x3.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="Dark spots before and after model" class="w-full h-auto object-cover rounded-2xl shadow-sm fk-disable-lazy" href="" id="cc-id-QQR8YmyIlrMz" title="" onclick="" target="_self" align="center" width="" height=""><div class="absolute bottom-6 right-6 bg-white/95 backdrop-blur px-6 py-3 rounded-lg text-sm font-bold shadow-lg text-coco-pink border border-pink-100 uppercase tracking-widest" href="" id="cc-id-mu6G46DCTqIg">
                                Real Results
                              </div></div><!-- Hero Image --><!-- STORY BODY --><div class="text-2xl leading-relaxed text-gray-800 max-w-5xl mx-auto" href="" id="cc-id-DNHoaGWuvc6K"><p class="mb-10" href="" id="cc-id-Hx8mcftMUZ49" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1776929417070_1774366422059_1772217487392_1771601008167_elementor_placeholder_image_1_.png"><span class="text-7xl float-left mr-4 mt-[-12px] font-serif font-bold text-black" href="" id="cc-id-qItLUmXOTRLG">I</span>
                                've spent 30 years looking at skin up close.
                              </p><p class="mb-10" href="" id="cc-id-unL3kb1Nqf65">
                                Models. Executives.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-8jfeuGLzrLeT"><strong href="" id="cc-id-2TBRN6LUy4Sk" data-layer-name="Text"></strong></p><p class="mb-10" href="" id="cc-id-Y9lAiNFjxsGL">
                                Women in their 60s who still get carded as a
                                joke.
                              </p><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-YuGkVqGnIgF6">
                                Women in their 40s who look two decades older
                                than they are.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-fltBL7Od9DXM"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Oxj3N96rrkMc"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-0esKY2fpcDKT"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2pj5fE9igzdg">
                                And the one thing that comes up more than
                                anything else…<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Twrx3j3CErFs"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-hK3k9GGkicwJ"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ZOusDilzejmR"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Jlq5AfHbEru6">
                                More than wrinkles, more than sagging
                                <b id="cc-id-CuPhNXYZLjJX" class="rte-styled-text">— is dark spots.</b><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-9QUOiOrei8lY"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-XH8r4tbP1mk3"><b class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-9BbudVoGZlYw"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-gL7Ft4pSeNoE"></b></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WboU6l5F79bX"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-VlbvpFPD1DBi">Because there's a particular cruelty to
                                  them.</span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-kZ1aQdbcaZGD"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-pVeUtb1i9FSf"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qJp4HSy1PdM3"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Ms1y3jmAvaXy"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-KTpdfbI2v9dc">You look at them and your mind goes straight
                                  to every summer you didn't wear sunscreen.
                                  Every beach trip. Every afternoon in the
                                  garden. Things you did when nobody told you
                                  any better — or when you were just living your
                                  life like everyone else around you.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-VdijO7aJDclc"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ORDO5Q3YLaHT"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-wi04ICPQwYSS"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-SUHddlCwfTwh"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-BV0abcXRdX43"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-enGx4gSQRIuf">So you try things. Vitamin C serums.
                                  Brightening creams. SPF every single day. That
                                  retinol everyone swears by.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-kBCjeix2MiTQ"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-G7GMpwfADzEU"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-WzEJE9yTstgU"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-QcwUPusbpqHX"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-687zN3gdJbcb"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qvIdutry94WH">And still — they're there.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-XCaFwZORdEBR"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-VySNt3cT5O7q"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-HxkEtncY1OsY"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Xulap1Kx0knN"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-xUyD01EceJvh"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-OKiJYeavDloJ">If that sounds familiar, I need you to hear
                                  this:<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-lcWMnAQIHBv2"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ZAeOczAKHL3r"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-quQmcnArTTZB"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-abJPb3394iGz"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-6gTKpumIgvAt"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-dlsUP8itC5tk"><b id="cc-id-Udk6saITvi1u" class="rte-styled-text">It's not your fault.</b><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-EldEPgPvMcvZ"></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ZXOxDeLD2dLM"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-pqnUecxM4AuC"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-8TgXB8beikQ5"><b class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-KQcbaXM3SGAw"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-4QpfQJwHEhsF"></b></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ODM3NvlgpYFH"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-us2bJnKTvbns"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Sf1VkmWduFwv">You've been trying to solve the right
                                    problem with the wrong approach.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-EYAfV6ncTI63"></span></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-dluDbD3zimGz"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-gw7BV4EI1MIz"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-mDunyfr0sY8b"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vl5qenSEl2oI"></span></span></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-IlyrLqYrTSRG"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-S4VFFh4meRw7"><span class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-xK7Xwn6z0T8R">And there's one reason — one specific
                                    reason — those spots keep coming back no
                                    matter what you put on them…<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-NxniiJEekYIw"></span></span></div><p id="cc-id-17JjsFDbKKYm"></p><div class="mb-12 pl-8 border-l-[10px] border-red-400 italic text-gray-600 bg-red-50 py-8 pr-8 rounded-r-2xl text-3xl" href="" id="cc-id-lapXt73U6g02" data-cc-mobile="false" data-cc-mobilelarge="false" data-cc-tablet="false" data-cc-tabletlarge="false" data-cc-desktop="false">
                                "I was terrified. I have extremely sensitive
                                skin. Most products burned me or caused a rash,
                                leaving the spot even darker than before."
                              </div><!-- Subheading --><h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-8 text-gray-900 serif-font" href="" id="cc-id-gvjqIhvzyEBs" data-src="https://assets.checkoutchamp.com/c8d59bb7-5ed4-4048-a389-a7ec37b55601/1776929417070_1774366422059_1772217487392_1771601008167_elementor_placeholder_image_1_.png">
                                You're treating dark spots like a skin problem.
                                They're not.
                              </h2><img class="fk-image-defaults" src="{{ '1778134075028_before_shot_5.webp' | asset_url }}" id="cc-id-6K6jBR6TTTU7" title="" href="" onclick="" target="_self" alt="" align="center" width="" height="" loading="lazy"><!-- VISUAL DEMO --><div class="my-12" href="" id="cc-id-D4zRtwQwBtkA"></div><p class="mb-10" href="" id="cc-id-N5ZVhlFMKgWf">
                                My name is Dr. Sarah Mitchell. I'm a
                                board-certified dermatologist with over 30 years
                                specializing in skin aging, pigmentation, and
                                cosmetic skin health.
                              </p><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-fwUN0rl4kh66">
                                What I'm about to share might make some very
                                powerful skincare companies very
                                uncomfortable.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-hG4fbaN2K5N4"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-yRoiEDyPZKtb"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-mnnXdfneWRBc"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ARLKWmJruRMp"><b id="cc-id-yHUysbahSuoQ" class="rte-styled-text">I've already had colleagues tell me to keep
                                  quiet about it.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-inigKCxXf8op"></b></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-B8ierLOyIVoP"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-fKNlW28HynVA"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-OEmwMoHNW1po">
                                But after three decades of watching women waste
                                thousands of dollars on products that were never
                                going to work — and knowing exactly why — I
                                can't stay silent anymore.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-gIQgC1yQksdh"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-g3StLj95tpI5"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UpyMYY59KfaP"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-KaMAsrX3vlzp">
                                One of my long-term patients, Patricia,
                                struggled with stubborn dark spots even though
                                she did
                                <b id="cc-id-wSLmOtBbK2Ya" class="rte-styled-text">“everything right.”</b><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-zrZiDhCzjNeO"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-MgN7dg4GjRH3"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-eZQZSskDqTBM"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-ODjkO5GBjumv">
                                At 67, she was the kind of woman who had never
                                skipped a skincare step in her life. SPF every
                                morning without fail. Vitamin C serum. A
                                brightening cream that cost her $140 a jar.
                                Regular facials. She was more disciplined than
                                women half her age.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-fHCW17iq83rk"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-I7lxPJrtTf1k"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-1tegbti6WqMh"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-qnNj5UqyuVZ2">
                                And still, the spots kept spreading.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-n6NIhJEfWZmI"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-xJnVMAORXxkN"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-GkmZrf1x5wXO"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-wHeODDSpYqfu">
                                Her cheeks. Her hands. The backs of her arms.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-xXPZZL7DfKSF"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UFxcELlJNjTe"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-b55mi3azn3YP"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Z4oPnPgzVoQE">
                                Every year, a little darker. A little more of
                                them.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-movmHFfbdLkb"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-zPHAJJtUwidZ"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-vYFgLFo8QDyE"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-UYkF4kkG4S8W">
                                She stopped wearing sleeveless tops.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-NgbYfnoHAxRS"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-THFDxf4zWXuP"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Cn491iw6ri7W"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-cL05cnBnbZU8">
                                Started keeping her hands in her lap during
                                dinners.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-bGXniP6DEmJE"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-CXOVPwzJl1Xt"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Q4wYWsriK9id"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-2PLpkK6geAoF">
                                Asked to be the one holding the camera, to avoid
                                being in the photos.<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-FpCwMhxoEw5W"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-Hh876vfXK4p2"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-1v6dVFLsbsI6"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-xxW8H6bOXxmL">
                                Then one evening, she and her husband went out
                                for their anniversary dinner…<br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-8VqezbaV90SK"></div><div class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-W0lujcVu5MaM"><br class="rte-styled-text" id="cc-id-tpqHVwiPfWJE"></div><p id="cc-id-VxQQyN571jiU"></p><img class="fk-image-defaults" src="{{ '1777471148987__1.webp' | asset_url }}" id="cc-id-OgeKPy2qxVt2" title="" href="" onclick="" target="_self" alt="" align="center" width="" height="" loading="lazy"><!-- Subheading --><p class="mb-10" href="" id="cc-id-PpYnHJ0DsFJj">
                                Candlelight, nice restaurant, the works.
